Checks verbatim token replacement, defaults and named arguments, empty
values, adjacent special tokens, SHIFT invalidation, nested IRP loops,
IRPN iteration changes and tuple padding, and output buffer growth/reuse.
Expected bytes are specified independently; the prior sequential build
must produce the same output.
control-args.inc deliberately contains literal bytes $1e,$01,$03 inside
the first argument, testing sequential fallback when it introduces token 2.
